<article class="env-definition" id="03XZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03XZ">Definition <span data-tag="03XZ">80.4.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $a : F \to G$ be a map of presheaves on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ which is representable by algebraic spaces. Let $\mathcal{P}$ be a property of morphisms of algebraic spaces which </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
is preserved under any base change, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
is fppf local on the base, see Descent on Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/03YH" data-tag="03YH">74.10.1</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In this case we say that $a$ has <em>property $\mathcal{P}$</em> if for every scheme $U$ and $\xi : U \to G$ the resulting morphism of algebraic spaces $U \times _ G F \to U$ has property $\mathcal{P}$. </p>
</article>